{"abstract":[{"text":"OpenID Connect surface controls (X7 G8, plan §4.6\/§4.8; T21.4). Settings that are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"password rules, here because this is the org-baseline-plus-tenant-override surface every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other per-tenant control lives on. They are not all of the same kind as each other, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is which is the whole of what [","type":"text"},{"code":"validate_tenant_override","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"clamp_overrides_to_org","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] read, so it is set out rather than inferred. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant may be stricter than its organization and never more permissive: *","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], validated ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — the mirror image of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"mfa_enforced","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because releasing personal data is the less-restrictive direction, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant can turn its organization’s decision off but never on. * [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::saml_idp_enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"],","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"validated ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" exactly like [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] (D-20): a tenant","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"may turn its organization’s ","type":"text"},{"cod